---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const updated = "June 7, 2026";

const toc = [
  { id: "acceptance", label: "Acceptance" },
  { id: "accounts", label: "Accounts" },
  { id: "uploads", label: "Uploading pets" },
  { id: "license", label: "Content & license" },
  { id: "community-content", label: "Community content" },
  { id: "acceptable-use", label: "Acceptable use" },
  { id: "operator-rights", label: "Operator rights" },
  { id: "disclaimer", label: "Disclaimer" },
  { id: "changes", label: "Changes" },
  { id: "contact", label: "Contact" },
];
---

<Base
  active=""
  title="Terms of Service — Codogotchi"
  description="The terms for using the Codogotchi pet gallery: account rules, what you may upload, the license you grant, and the operator's right to unlist any pet."
>
  <div class="max-w-7xl w-full mx-auto px-6 py-8 flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-6">
    <!-- Sidebar -->
    <aside class="hidden md:block w-60 flex-shrink-0">
      <div class="sticker-card bg-surface-container-lowest rounded-2xl p-5 sticky top-24">
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-bold mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-secondary">gavel</span>
          Terms
        </h3>
        <ul class="flex flex-col gap-2">
          {
            toc.map((t) => (
              <li>
                <a
                  href={`#${t.id}`}
                  class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant hover:text-primary font-medium"
                >
                  {t.label}
                </a>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="flex-grow min-w-0 flex flex-col gap-8">
      <!-- Hero -->
      <section
        class="sticker-card bg-surface-container-low rounded-2xl p-8 relative overflow-hidden"
      >
        <span
          class="material-symbols-outlined absolute -top-3 -right-3 text-6xl text-surface-variant opacity-40 rotate-12"
          >gavel</span
        >
        <h1 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold mb-3">
          Terms of Service
        </h1>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant max-w-2xl mb-2">
          These terms cover the Codogotchi pet
          <a href="/gallery" class="text-primary font-bold underline">gallery</a> —
          a community marketplace where creators upload and share desktop-pet
          packages. By using the gallery you agree to them. They are written in
          plain language for a small, owner-operated project; please read our
          <a href="/privacy" class="text-primary font-bold underline">Privacy Policy</a
          > alongside them.
        </p>
        <p class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant/70">Last updated: {updated}</p>
      </section>

      <!-- Acceptance -->
      <section id="acceptance" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Acceptance</h2>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
          By browsing, downloading, or uploading pets you accept these terms. If
          you do not agree, do not use the gallery. You must be old enough to form a
          binding agreement in your jurisdiction to create an account.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Accounts -->
      <section id="accounts" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Accounts</h2>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
          You may browse and install pets without an account. To upload a pet you
          sign in with Google, GitHub, or an email and password, and choose a public
          username. You are responsible for activity under your account and for
          keeping your credentials secure. Pick a username that does not impersonate
          someone else.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Uploads -->
      <section id="uploads" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Uploading pets</h2>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed mb-3">
          When you upload a pet you confirm that you created it or otherwise have the
          right to share it, and that it does not infringe anyone's intellectual
          property or other rights.
        </p>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
          Every upload is validated on the server, stripped to an allowlist of
          expected files, and re-packed into a canonical package before it is stored
          or made available for download. Uploads that fail validation are rejected.
          This protects downloaders, but it does not make us the author of, or
          responsible for, the artwork or content you submit.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- License -->
      <section id="license" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Content &amp; license</h2>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
          You keep ownership of the pets you create. By publishing a pet to the
          gallery you grant Codogotchi a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free
          license to host, store, reformat (including the server re-pack and
          thumbnail generation), display, and distribute that pet so that others can
          view and install it. This license lasts while the pet is listed and ends
          when the pet is removed, except for copies already downloaded by others.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Community content -->
      <section id="community-content" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Community content</h2>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
          Pets in the gallery are community-shared and may be inspired by existing
          characters or brands. Codogotchi does not claim rights to any character
          designs shown here, and listing a pet is not an endorsement. If you believe
          a pet infringes your rights, email
          <a href="mailto:admin@codogotchi.app" class="text-primary font-bold underline"
            >admin@codogotchi.app</a
          > with enough detail to identify the pet and we will review and, where
          appropriate, unlist it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Acceptable use -->
      <section id="acceptable-use" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Acceptable use</h2>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed mb-2">You agree not to:</p>
        <ul
          class="flex flex-col gap-2 text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5"
        >
          <li>
            Upload malware, exploits, or anything designed to harm a downloader's
            machine.
          </li>
          <li>Upload content you do not have the right to share.</li>
          <li>
            Upload illegal, hateful, harassing, or sexually explicit content, or
            content that targets or endangers others.
          </li>
          <li>
            Impersonate another person or misrepresent your affiliation with anyone.
          </li>
          <li>
            Abuse, probe, or attempt to disrupt the service, or evade the upload
            validation and re-pack pipeline.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Operator rights -->
      <section id="operator-rights" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Operator rights</h2>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
          We may unlist or remove any pet, and suspend or remove any account, at any
          time and at our discretion — for example for a takedown request, a terms
          violation, or a safety concern. Unlisting is immediate: the pet disappears
          from the gallery and its download endpoints. We are not obligated to host
          any particular pet.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Disclaimer -->
      <section id="disclaimer" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Disclaimer</h2>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
          The gallery and all pets are provided <strong>as is</strong>, without
          warranties of any kind. Pets are made by the community; we validate
          packages for structural safety but do not guarantee their quality,
          accuracy, or fitness for any purpose. To the maximum extent permitted by
          law, Codogotchi is not liable for any damages arising from your use of the
          gallery or any pet you install.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Changes -->
      <section id="changes" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Changes</h2>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
          We may update these terms as the project evolves. When we do, we will
          update the date at the top of this page. Continued use after a change means
          you accept the updated terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Contact -->
      <section id="contact" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <div
          class="bg-primary-fixed text-on-primary-fixed-variant rounded-xl border-2 border-charcoal-ink p-5 flex items-start gap-3"
        >
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined">mail</span>
          <p class="text-sm">
            Questions or takedowns:
            <a href="mailto:admin@codogotchi.app" class="font-bold underline"
              >admin@codogotchi.app</a
            >. See also our <a href="/privacy" class="font-bold underline"
              >Privacy Policy</a
            >.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
